            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> If you ask for my opinion:\n> If language level is 2, exceptions can be interpreted the way they are right now.\n> If language level is set to 3: The Cython Interpreter should conform to the Python 3 Syntax.\n\nYes. That probably should have been true but it's a breaking change now.\n\n> BTW: It seems like the Cython Codebase is suffering from this ambigouity itself https://github.com/cython/cython/blob/master/Cython/Runtime/refnanny.pyx#L137.\n\nYes - we should (and will) have to update that. But it's a good example of how there's existing code out there and giving people a warning before changing it is now necessary.",
